#3DBenchy - The jolly 3D printing torture-test by CreativeTools.se - 763622 - part 1 of 2.zip

# Python bytecode cache (never commit — regenerated locally, and machine-
# generated .pyc files were previously (wrongly) tracked; see TODO.md / CI fix
# notes for the removal commit)
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo

# Python virtual environments (never commit).  The local .venv here is 351 MB of
# third-party packages; a single `git add -A` would push the lot.  Nothing under
# it has ever been tracked, so this is a guard rather than a cleanup.
#
# It also matters to CI: `.github/workflows/ci.yml` runs `flake8` with an
# explicit --exclude list that does NOT name .venv, so lint only passes today
# because CI checks out a fresh tree with no virtualenv in it.  Were one ever
# committed, the lint job would immediately fail on thousands of findings in
# vendored code.  (Locally, `flake8 .` does report those — run it over
# `git ls-files '*.py'` instead to see only this repo's own code.)
#
# NOTE for anyone running the tools: this .venv SHADOWS system Python packages
# the repo's tools rely on (manifold3d, sympy, matplotlib are installed
# system-wide).  Invoke tools as `/usr/bin/python3 tools/<name>.py`, not through
# the venv.
.venv/
venv/
env/
ENV/

# Claude Code agent worktrees and session data
.claude/

# FreeCAD large binary outputs (exceed GitHub 100 MB limit — use LFS if needed)
*.FCBak
*.FCStd

